== Notable people ==
* {{nihongo|[[Hayashi Kenjirō]]|林 健二郎}} – Founder of [[Fukushima Fire Industries]] and inventor of the modern commercial hot sauce production process (1889–1967)
* {{nihongo|[[Matsumoto Chiyo]]|松本 千代}} – Agricultural scientist who developed the Fukushima Dragon pepper cultivar through selective breeding (1912–1998)
* {{nihongo|[[Takahashi Isamu]]|高橋 勇}} – Celebrity chef and television personality known for popularizing spicy cuisine throughout Okaiken (born 1954)
* {{nihongo|[[Watanabe Yuki]]|渡辺 雪}} – Industrial chemist who pioneered capsaicin extraction methods for pharmaceutical applications (born 1968)
* {{nihongo|[[Kobayashi Hideo]]|小林 秀夫}} – Professional competitive eater, six-time champion of the Fukushima Fire Festival's Dragon's Challenge (born 1982)
* {{nihongo|[[Yamamoto Sakurako]]|山本 桜子}} – Master pepper weaver and designated Living National Treasure for her work in traditional chili crafts (born 1945)
* {{nihongo|[[Sato Masahiro]]|佐藤 正弘}} – Food scientist and current director of the [[Fukushima Chili Genome Project]] (born 1971)
* {{nihongo|[[Inoue Kohana]]|井上 小花}} – Chef-owner of [[Dragon's Breath]], the prefecture's first restaurant to receive three Michelin stars for spicy cuisine (born 1988)
* {{nihongo|[[Nakamura Tsuyoshi]]|中村 剛}} – Chief executive of [[Kōrēgusu Distillers]] and philanthropist supporting agricultural education (born 1962)
* {{nihongo|[[Aoki Rina]]|青木 里奈}} – Folklorist and author documenting the oral traditions of Fukushima's spice farming communities (born 1978)

